Package: rtdo
Version: 0.5.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libpam0g, systemd
Maintainer: Reimilia617 <Reimilia617@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Reimilia617/RTDO-Project
Description: Root Task Do — interactive, policy-driven privilege elevation tool (sudo alternative)
 rtdo is a policy-driven, environment-adaptive sudo alternative. It authenticates
 against the root password (PAM), then decides per command whether to allow, prompt,
 or block based on trusted paths and a blacklist.
 .
 On first run it auto-detects a missing or weak root password (equal to any username
 or any user's password) and guides you through setting a new one. It can optionally
 disable sudo via a Go daemon (rtdo-sudod, systemd service) that intercepts `sudo`
 and tells you to use rtdo; use `sudo-force` for the original sudo. All output is
 bilingual (Chinese/English), following LANG.
